1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,400
We're now going to look at how to view and remove existing extensions.

2
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:16,000
To see information about the installed extensions available in your library, log in to Burp

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Suite Enterprise as an administrator or an account that has been given permissions to

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,760
manage extensions.

5
00:00:22,760 --> 00:00:26,240
From the settings menu, choose extensions.

6
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:34,140
To display the list of current extensions, select BAP extensions or custom extensions.

7
00:00:34,140 --> 00:00:42,680
To see a description of an extension, click on the question mark for help.

8
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:49,200
To delete an extension, again, log in as an administrator or account with suitable permissions.

9
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:52,200
From the settings menu, choose extensions.

10
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:55,920
Click on the tab for the type of extension you want to delete.

11
00:00:55,920 --> 00:01:01,180
And click on the trash icon next to the extension.

12
00:01:01,180 --> 00:01:06,260
If you remove an extension whilst the scan that uses it is in progress, the scan continues

13
00:01:06,260 --> 00:01:13,260
to use the extension until it finishes.

14
00:01:13,260 --> 00:01:18,240
And click on the tab for the type of extension.

15
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:22,240
And click on the tab for the type of extension.

16
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:25,240
And click on the tab for the type of extension.

17
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:27,240
And click on the tab for the extension.

18
00:01:27,240 --> 00:01:29,240
And click on the tab for the extension.

19
00:01:29,240 --> 00:01:31,240
And click on the tab for the extension.

20
00:01:31,240 --> 00:01:33,240
And click on the tab for the extension.

21
00:01:33,240 --> 00:01:35,240
And click on the tab for the extension.

